NAME
    [ - evaluate a conditional expression

SYNOPSIS
    [ EXPR ]

DESCRIPTION
    Alias for test(1). Evaluates EXPR and sets the exit status to 0 when
    true or 1 when false. A literal closing ']' argument is required.

EXAMPLES
    if [ -f /Logs/run.log ]; then echo found; fi
    [ "$COUNT" -gt 0 ] && echo non-zero

EXIT STATUS
    0   EXPR evaluates to true.
    1   EXPR evaluates to false, is empty, or is missing the closing ']'.

SEE ALSO
    test(1), if(1), while(1)
